{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אך את שבתותי תשמורו", :translit "akh et shabtotai tishmeru", :gloss "Only My Sabbaths you shall keep"} {:he "אך", :translit "akh", :gloss "only / however"} {:he "פיקוח נפש", :translit "pikuach nefesh", :gloss "danger to life"} {:he "קרבנות צבור", :translit "korbanot tzibur", :gloss "communal offerings"} {:he "מלאכת שבת", :translit "melakht shabbat", :gloss "labors of Sabbath"} {:he "מלאכת המשכן", :translit "melakht hamishkan", :gloss "labors of the Tabernacle"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "ריבוי/מיעוט: the word אך functions as a restrictive particle (mi'ut), limiting the Sabbath prohibition to permit certain overrides"} {:kind :other, :note "סמיכות: juxtaposition of the Sabbath pericope to the Tabernacle labors forms the hermeneutical basis for deriving the 39 Sabbath labors"}], :frame {:text "The word אך serves as a mi'ut (restrictive particle) excluding pikuach nefesh and communal offerings from the Sabbath prohibition; these overrides are treated in Shabbat 132a–133a and the principle that communal offerings override the Sabbath at Shabbat 132b. The 39 labors forbidden on Sabbath are derived from the 39 labors of the Tabernacle: just as the Tabernacle labor ceased on Sabbath, so all categories enumerated in connection with it define Sabbath rest (Shabbat 49b, 97b). The juxtaposition of the Sabbath pericope to the Tabernacle section in Exodus 31:13 provides the textual anchor for this derivation.", :sources ["Exodus 31:13" "Shabbat 49b" "Shabbat 97b" "Shabbat 132a" "Shabbat 132b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "ריבוי/מיעוט: the word אך functions as a restrictive particle (mi'ut), limiting the Sabbath prohibition to permit certain overrides", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "סמיכות: juxtaposition of the Sabbath pericope to the Tabernacle labors forms the hermeneutical basis for deriving the 39 Sabbath labors", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:25.038285044Z", :model "glm-5.2"}